      "title": "The Unspoken",
      "category": "Poetry",
      "date": "2026-11-13",
      "summary": "I am not broken, I am just tired.",
      "image": "",
      "body": "I have no reason to be sad,\nyet my chest feels heavy.\nLike clouds have gathered in the sky,\nbut the rain refuses to fall.\nIt wants to pour, but it cannot.\n\nI smile, I talk, I blend in with everyone —\nbut at the end of the day, when I am alone,\nI feel like a stranger to myself.\nAs if I am lost inside my own soul.\n\nI want to tell someone,\n\"You know, I don't feel good.\"\nBut what will I say? I don't even know why I don't feel good.\nI just know, something is missing.\nSomething that was supposed to be here,\nis not here anymore.\n\nMaybe I am not missing someone,\nI am missing me.\nThe me who used to be happy with so little.\nThe me who used to laugh with an open heart,\nand cry with an open soul.\n\nNow I just stay silent.\nBecause even tears need a language,\nand my tears have no language.\nMy pain has no name.\n\nI am not broken,\nI am just tired.\nTired of being strong for so long.\nTired of saying \"I am fine\" for so long.\n\nIf just once, someone came and said,\n\"It's okay, you don't have to be strong.\"\nThen maybe this gathered cloud\nwould finally fall as rain."
